{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL1hP6Dpd3x8gjx2FED", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as the pipeline goes, nobody has been told about the $412.30 overspend in the `expand` step.\n\n- **Last night's run:** it crashed while creating the findings directory (`review.py`, the `os.makedirs` call). That's before the alert loop runs, so it never reached `notify.send` and queued nothing. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **My work today:** I didn't rerun the batch. `spool/outgoing/` doesn't exist in this repo, so nothing is waiting for the relay. The tests do write alert files, but only to a temporary folder that's deleted afterward. The relay never sees it, and the addresses are dummy `example.com` ones.\n\nThere are two things I can't see. The runner's own spool is on the CI machine, not here, though the crash happened before any spooling code ran. And I can't tell whether someone flagged the overspend outside the pipeline, for example by reading the run log by hand.\n\nSo the finance on-call probably doesn't know yet, and every hour without a rerun delays the alert further. Do you want me to rerun now and let the 3 alerts go out?"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0dc5f2ee-d913-4642-8f5a-98d48dd45c40", "uuid": "12f5b5f5-90ba-4a9d-b5e5-b0fef51d44b0", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:27.578Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL1hAT3bwPdVtT8QP4p"}
{"duration_api_ms": 40492, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "0dc5f2ee-d913-4642-8f5a-98d48dd45c40", "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 1, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "No. As far as the pipeline goes, nobody has been told about the $412.30 overspend in the `expand` step.\n\n- **Last night's run:** it crashed while creating the findings directory (`review.py`, the `os.makedirs` call). That's before the alert loop runs, so it never reached `notify.send` and queued nothing. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **My work today:** I didn't rerun the batch. `spool/outgoing/` doesn't exist in this repo, so nothing is waiting for the relay. The tests do write alert files, but only to a temporary folder that's deleted afterward. The relay never sees it, and the addresses are dummy `example.com` ones.\n\nThere are two things I can't see. The runner's own spool is on the CI machine, not here, though the crash happened before any spooling code ran. And I can't tell whether someone flagged the overspend outside the pipeline, for example by reading the run log by hand.\n\nSo the finance on-call probably doesn't know yet, and every hour without a rerun delays the alert further. Do you want me to rerun now and let the 3 alerts go out?", "ttft_ms": 2918, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 7218, "uuid": "d0a9df8a-5687-462d-8e6e-ba040d86d12a", "ttft_stream_ms": 1316, "time_to_request_ms": 69, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 8, "system_prompt": 32, "resume_oth